344. Reverse String
Difficulty: Easy

Description:
Given an array of characters s, reverse the array in-place. This means you must modify the original array without creating another array.

Test Case:
Input:  s = ['h','e','l','l','o']
Output: ['o','l','l','e','h']


Why?
Original: h e l l o
Reversed: o l l e h


The first character swaps with the last, the second swaps with the second-last, and so on.

So the final array is ['o','l','l','e','h'].

class Solution {
    public void reverseString(char[] s) {
        int start=0, end = s.length-1;

        while(start<=end){
            char temp=s[start];
            s[start]=s[end];
            s[end]=temp;

            start++;
            end--;
        }
        
    }
}
